<p>Social Circus started with a simple annoyance: every "best icebreaker questions" list online reads like it was written for a corporate retreat nobody wanted to attend. We wanted something better — tools you can actually use in the two minutes before a meeting starts or a party goes quiet.</p>

<p>So that's what we built. Four free, interactive tools — an icebreaker generator, a party game picker, a team-building activity finder, and a conversation starter wheel — plus a growing library of guides for planning game nights, meetings, and get-togethers that people actually enjoy.</p>

<h2>What we believe about a good icebreaker</h2>
<p>It should be specific enough to answer easily, open enough to lead somewhere interesting, and never, ever require a trust fall. That's the filter every question, game, and activity on this site has to pass.</p>

<h2>No sign-up, ever</h2>
<p>Every tool on Social Circus runs entirely in your browser — no accounts, no email capture, no data collection beyond standard anonymous site analytics. Pick a tool, get an idea, use it.</p>

<h2>How the site is funded</h2>
<p>Social Circus is supported by display advertising and affiliate links to products we think are genuinely useful for game night or team events. Full details are in our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>

<p>Got a question, a game we should add, or feedback on a tool? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>.</p>
